### Summary / Symptom
Agents are reporting that searching for contacts by phone number returns no results even when the number exists in the system. The same contact is found correctly when searching by name. This started after last Friday's maintenance window and is affecting all agency staff.

### Resolution
The root cause was a database index for phone number search rebuilt with a case-sensitive collation and without normalizing phone number formatting, causing queries to miss matches with different formats. To resolve this, the index was rebuilt using a case-insensitive collation, and a normalization step was added to strip formatting characters from phone numbers before searching. This restored correct search functionality for all agency staff. Future maintenance should ensure both collation and normalization are properly configured for search indexes.


