### Summary / Symptom
Integration between Guidewire and the third-party telematics provider is dropping 15-20% of incoming driving score payloads. Affected policies are not receiving their safe-driver discount adjustments. The issue appears intermittent and does not produce any error logs on the Guidewire side.

### Resolution
The integration with a third-party telematics provider was intermittently dropping 15-20% of incoming driving score payloads, resulting in missed safe-driver discounts. The root cause was a schema change by the provider, adding a new required field ('deviceFirmwareVersion') that the Guidewire integration adapter was not mapping, causing silent discards. The resolution involved updating the adapter's mapping configuration to include the new field, implementing a dead-letter queue for future unmapped payloads, and reprocessing the previously dropped payloads from the provider's retry queue.


